  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is participating in a race of YYY kilometers. However, Chef gets tired and needs to take a rest after every XXX kilometers.\n\nCan you determine how many times Chef will stop to rest before reaching the finish line?\n\n\nInput Format\nThe only line of input contains two space-separated integers XXX and YYY — the number of kilometers Chef can run before needing a rest, and the total distance of the race in kilometers.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint a single integer — the number of times Chef will stop to rest before completing the race.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X,Y≤101 \\leq X,Y \\leq 101≤X,Y≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 2",
        "output": "1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAfter running the first kilometer, Chef gets tired and stops to rest. After resting, he completes the remaining kilometer to finish the race. Since he stops only once before reaching the finish line, the answer is 111."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 5",
        "output": "2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAfter running the first 222 kilometers, Chef gets tired and takes a rest. He then runs another 222 kilometers and rests again. Finally, he completes the remaining 111 kilometer to finish the race. Since he stops twice before reaching the finish line, the answer is 222."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3 3",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAfter running the first 333 kilometers, he reaches the finish line without needing to rest."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_4",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4 3",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nSince the total distance is less than the resting limit, Chef reaches the finish line without stopping."
      }
    ]
  },
